            <ArticleTitle>Dangerous single lead ST elevation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111.e1-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jelectrocard.2008.10.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Discriminating among the various coronary obstruction patterns influences early management decisions. One of the most important tasks is the identification of ST-elevation myocardial infarction caused by left main occlusion. We present a case of single-lead ST-segment elevation in aVR caused by acute left main coronary artery occlusion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
